        "procedure": "In a glovebox under nitrogen, trimethylaluminum (86.0 mg, 1.19 mmol) was added to an ether solution (5 mL) of [Cp'Tm(CH2SiMe3)2(THF)] (1-Tm) (728 mg, 1.19 mmol) in a 30 mL flask. The main text reports that the analogous room-temperature reaction of 1-Tm with AlMe3 affords 3-Tm in 68% yield, and that 2-Tm releases CH4 on warming to room temperature to give 3-Tm. After stirring at room temperature for 2 h, the solvent was removed under vacuum, the residue was extracted with hexane and filtered, and slow evaporation gave pink crystals of 3-Tm (315 mg, 68% yield).",
