      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "In a glovebox, a benzene solution (5 mL) of [Cp'Tm(μ2-Me)2]3 (2-Tm) (235 mg, 0.200 mmol) was transferred to a 30 mL Schlenk tube, taken outside the glovebox, and stirred at 90 °C for 2 h. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, the residue was extracted with hexane and filtered, and the solvent was again removed. Recrystallization from benzene gave light-green crystals of 4-Tm·(C6H6)2 (247 mg, 99% yield). The SI also states that heating 3-Tm in benzene at 90 °C for 2 h gives 4-Tm quantitatively. The main text reports the same 90 °C thermolysis of 2-Tm or 3-Tm in quantitative yield but without a numerical reagent amount.",
