        "procedure": "In a glovebox, a J. Young NMR tube was charged with 4-Lu (64 mg, 0.040 mmol), C6D6 (0.45 mL), and benzaldehyde or benzophenone (0.16 mmol). 1H NMR monitoring showed quantitative formation of Cp'4Lu4O4 (5-Lu) and the corresponding alkene CH2=CRR' within 10 min at room temperature. 5-Lu was identified by comparison of NMR and X-ray data with the previously reported complex and was not given a new CCDC deposition in this paper. The main text describes the same rapid room-temperature reaction in benzene without numerical amounts.",
